---
/**
 * A cantilever: fixed at one end only (wall), loaded at the free end.
 * Matches the SKILLS SK1 worked example: a 150 mm arm carrying 40 N,
 * giving a 6 N·m reaction moment at the fixed end — contrast with
 * BeamReactionsDiagram's simply-supported beam, which shares the load
 * between two supports and has no reaction moment.
 */
const caption =
  'A cantilever arm, 150 mm long, fixed into a wall at one end and free at the other. A 40 N load at the free end must be resisted entirely by the fixed end: an upward reaction force of 40 N, and a reaction moment of 6 N·m — because there is no second support to share either with.';
---

<figure class="diagram">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 420 210" role="img" aria-labelledby="cl-t cl-d" class="dg">
    <title id="cl-t">A cantilever arm fixed at one end</title>
    <desc id="cl-d">{caption}</desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="cl-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="fill-accent" />
      </marker>
      <marker id="cl-arrow2" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="fill-accent2" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- Fixed wall support: hatched block -->
    <rect x="24" y="40" width="18" height="120" class="wall" />
    <line x1="24" y1="50" x2="42" y2="35" class="hatch" />
    <line x1="24" y1="70" x2="42" y2="55" class="hatch" />
    <line x1="24" y1="90" x2="42" y2="75" class="hatch" />
    <line x1="24" y1="110" x2="42" y2="95" class="hatch" />
    <line x1="24" y1="130" x2="42" y2="115" class="hatch" />
    <line x1="24" y1="150" x2="42" y2="135" class="hatch" />
    <line x1="24" y1="165" x2="42" y2="150" class="hatch" />

    <!-- Cantilever arm -->
    <rect x="42" y="95" width="270" height="10" class="beam" />

    <!-- Load at free end (down) -->
    <line x1="312" y1="35" x2="312" y2="91" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#cl-arrow)" />
    <text x="320" y="45" text-anchor="start">40 N</text>

    <!-- Reaction force at fixed end (up) -->
    <line x1="55" y1="165" x2="55" y2="109" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#cl-arrow)" />
    <text x="55" y="182" text-anchor="middle">R = 40 N</text>

    <!-- Reaction moment: curved arrow near the fixed end -->
    <path d="M 78,60 A 22,22 0 1 1 76,84" class="arrow2" marker-end="url(#cl-arrow2)" />
    <text x="112" y="76" text-anchor="start" class="accent2">M = 6 N·m</text>

    <!-- Span dimension -->
    <line x1="42" y1="130" x2="312" y2="130" class="dimline" />
    <line x1="42" y1="124" x2="42" y2="136" class="dimline" />
    <line x1="312" y1="124" x2="312" y2="136" class="dimline" />
    <text x="177" y="148" text-anchor="middle" class="dim">150 mm</text>

    <text x="33" y="30" text-anchor="middle" class="dim">Wall</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>{caption}</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .diagram { margin-block: 1.75rem; }
  .dg { width: 100%; height: auto; max-width: 440px; display: block; margin-inline: auto; }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .wall { fill: var(--bg-3); stroke: var(--text); stroke-width: 2; }
  .hatch { stroke: var(--text-faint); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .beam { fill: var(--bg-3); stroke: var(--text); stroke-width: 2; }
  .arrow { stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 2.5; fill: none; }
  .arrow2 { stroke: var(--accent-2); stroke-width: 2.5; fill: none; }
  .fill-accent { fill: var(--accent); }
  .fill-accent2 { fill: var(--accent-2); }
  .accent2 { fill: var(--accent-2); }
  .dimline { stroke: var(--text-faint); stroke-width: 1; }
  text { fill: var(--text-dim); font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 13px; }
  .dim { fill: var(--text-faint); font-size: 11px; }
</style>
